{"kind":"request","text":"Evidence-rules preparation decision before Source, as a53e1464 requires. J3 is accepted first and being implemented independently on Main 0881c1bc; this question does not hold it.\n\nThe first-slice design leaves the admin's room-service key mark and rotation open. Preparation now has a concrete minimum:\n\n1. The new Rules singleton owns at most one explicit roomService pair {checker: MemberRef, key: KeyId}, published only by an active admin through the native publish path. Null withdraws it; new genesis is unmarked. Retain a last-mark-change position scoped by the exact Rules ScopeRef/incarnation; preserve it when the pair is unchanged, change it on replacement or clear/re-add. The position is native-selected, not caller-chosen. Do not store the current publish's own full hash in its effects. Fresh native Rules observations bind the current mark/generation/head; any required full fact proof must come from already recorded bytes, not a self-hash.\n\n2. No grandfathering of unfinished room jobs: admission freezes the marked member/key and generation with the exact job/tree/configuration/source/stage. Once Destination observes rotation, neither old key nor new key can complete that old fence. A new explicitly requested fenced job is required; no automatic restart, re-sign, reuse or reclassification. Old accepted results remain historical. Reuse still checks today's eligible signer; audits always run fresh. Timing is the established bounded native observation order, not instantaneous cross-scope revocation at the Rules commit.\n\n3. Exact key/source enforcement is at Destination's existing native signed-result judge. The declared lane may retain an ordinarily member-authorized result which Destination refuses to count as wrong-source. This is a real boundary choice: current declared {signer:true} yields MemberRef, not actor KeyId, and observation rows are platform-only. A lane field claiming a key is no proof that key signed it.\n\nPlease approve or amend three points:\nA. Rules-owned admin mark with exact active-key ownership checked at every use. Current publish can observe an active checker MEMBER, not prove an arbitrary target KEY atomically at marking. Requiring that stronger marking-time property needs an additional native owner/exchange.\nB. No grandfathering after observed rotation, with the stated bounded observation order. If immediate global revocation at Rules commit is required, choose an explicit Destination-local fence/handshake.\nC. Destination wrong-source refusal-to-count is sufficient for the commissioned witness. If the lane's check act itself must refuse a wrong key, explicitly choose or commission the additional native exchange/guard mechanism; I will not silently add an actor-key DSL operand.\n\nSource facts read at 0881c1bca1df31a9fdb4ae72947cbbedf1b3ec51: packages/platform/src/rules-scope.ts (publish observes checker members, revisionOf uses local positions); packages/derive/src/guards.ts (ruleInput.signer); packages/platform/src/destination.ts (checked14 and CertifiedCheckProof inspect signed actor keys); notes/2026-10-16-evidence-rules-design.md (open source/rotation choices and Decisions). The preparation memo will record your disposition before native evidence-slice edits. No evidence native Source or deployment has started.","body":{"conditions":"Record the three concrete room-service key/rotation/wrong-source decisions below before evidence-rules source. This request owes a policy report, no Git artifact; J3 continues independently.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}